  "title": "Artifical Intelligence Podcast",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning make us look at human intelligence in a new light. In the podcast, we talk to the ETH professors Ben­jamin Grewe, Simone Schürle, and Thomas Hofmann about the advantages and the dangers of Artificial Intelligence. We also take a glimpse into the future and talk about new technologies such as little implants to enhance human brains. How much has fiction already become a reality?\n\nThis year's Scientifica , the Science Days of the University and ETH Zurich, from 30 August to 1 September, will also deal with the topic Science Fiction - Science Facts."
    }
  ],
